<h1>Meredith Sisnett</h1>
<p class="contact">Austin, TX</p>
<p class="contact">The Collaborative Advocate Foundation</p>

<h2>Project Role: Community Coordinator / Project Co-Director</h2>

<p>Community engagement and government operations professional with extensive experience in housing stability, displacement prevention, contract management, and organizational development within the City of Austin. Recognized by NAACP President Nelson Linder and MEASURE President Meme Styles for community service, civic engagement, and philanthropic leadership. Brings deep, lived understanding of the systemic barriers facing Austin's BIPOC communities -- housing insecurity, economic instability, and fragmented social services -- and translates that understanding into program design, community outreach, and partnership development at TCAF.</p>

<h2>Relevance to Sankofa Knowledge Systems Project</h2>

<ul>
<li>Leads TCAF's community outreach, participant recruitment, and integration of community voice into program design -- directly responsible for the community-led participatory research at the core of Pillar 1 (Knowledge Generation and Preservation)</li>
<li>Deep expertise in Austin's Eastern Crescent neighborhoods (ZIP codes 78702, 78721, 78741, 78744) where the Sankofa oral history documentation and CHW training will be conducted</li>
<li>Established relationships with community elders, neighborhood organizations, and civic institutions essential for culturally grounded knowledge collection and trust-building</li>
<li>Experience in contract management and compliance monitoring -- will oversee sub-agreements with three international partner organizations (Ghana, Brazil, Jamaica)</li>
<li>Understanding of housing instability and displacement as SDOH factors directly informs how diaspora health knowledge is contextualized within the Sankofa Health Network platform</li>
</ul>

<h2>Professional Experience</h2>

<h3>Community Coordinator -- The Collaborative Advocate Foundation | 2025-Present</h3>
<ul>
<li>Coordinates community outreach, participant recruitment, and stakeholder engagement across TCAF's 24-platform digital ecosystem</li>
<li>Integrates community voice and lived experience into platform design, content development, and program evaluation</li>
<li>Builds and maintains partnerships with Austin-area nonprofits, civic organizations, health providers, and educational institutions</li>
<li>Supports grant development by providing community context, needs assessment data, and stakeholder documentation</li>
</ul>

<h3>Contract Management Specialist III -- City of Austin, Housing Department | Displacement Prevention Division</h3>
<ul>
<li>Managed contract oversight, compliance monitoring, and coordination with housing service providers serving communities facing displacement due to gentrification and rising costs</li>
<li>Developed expertise in navigating government systems, regulatory requirements, and multi-stakeholder coordination -- skills directly applicable to managing international partnership agreements and grant compliance</li>
<li>Gained firsthand understanding of how housing instability drives health inequity, food insecurity, and educational disruption in Austin's historically Black and Latino neighborhoods</li>
</ul>

<h3>Organizational Development and Training Specialist -- City of Austin</h3>
<ul>
<li>Facilitated New Hire Orientation and Management Training programs, developing curricula and training delivery methods for diverse adult learners</li>
<li>Experience in curriculum design and training facilitation directly relevant to developing the Bidirectional Knowledge Exchange curriculum for CHWs</li>
<li>Built cross-departmental relationships and coordinated multi-stakeholder initiatives within complex government systems</li>
</ul>

<h2>Community Recognition and Leadership</h2>

<ul>
<li>Recognized by NAACP President Nelson Linder for community service and dedication to helping others</li>
<li>Recognized by MEASURE President Meme Styles for Community Engagement and Philanthropic efforts</li>
<li>Active engagement across Austin's nonprofit and civic sectors in community health, housing equity, and social services navigation</li>
</ul>

<h2>Core Competencies</h2>

<ul>
<li>Community Engagement and Participatory Research</li>
<li>Contract Management and Compliance Monitoring</li>
<li>Housing Stability and Displacement Prevention</li>
<li>Curriculum Design and Adult Training Facilitation</li>
<li>Stakeholder Coordination and Partnership Development</li>
<li>Social Services Navigation and SDOH Context</li>
<li>Program Design with Community Voice Integration</li>
</ul>

